WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.790
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:04.560
it.

3
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.300
Just follow along step by step. Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12

4
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.160
tablets each and

5
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.920
a measured container. Start your first dose between 6 and 7 p.m. the night

6
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.320
before your procedure.

7
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.310
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets. Fill the provided container with 16

8
00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:22.480
ounces of water up to

9
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.220
the fill line. Swallow one tablet every two minutes with a sip of water,

10
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.240
finishing all 12 tablets

11
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.230
over about 15 to 20 minutes. Take your time and go at a steady pace. About one

12
00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:34.480
hour after your last

13
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.240
tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces of water and drink the entire

14
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.200
amount slowly over

15
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.550
30 minutes. Then about 30 minutes after finishing that container, fill it one

16
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:44.640
more time with 16

17
00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.200
ounces of water and drink the entire amount over 30 minutes. That completes

18
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.040
your first dose.

19
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:55.620
Repeat the exact same three steps using your second bottle of 12 tablets. One

20
00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.080
tablet every

21
00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:00.320
two minutes with water, then 16 ounces of water one hour later, then 16 ounces

22
00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.440
of water, 30 minutes

23
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.650
after that. This part is really important. You must drink all of the prep

24
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:05.760
solution as directed,

25
00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.620
even if you're already passing clear liquid. I know it can feel like enough,

26
00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:10.320
but finishing the

27
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.300
entire dose is what gives us the clearest view during your procedure. If the

28
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.760
prep isn't completed as

29
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.480
directed, we may need to reschedule and neither of us wants that. Between doses

30
00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:20.960
, keep drinking

31
00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.440
clear liquids to stay hydrated. It will help you feel better and help the prep

32
00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:25.120
do its job.

33
00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.360
Do not drink anything at all within four hours of your procedure, including

34
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.240
water unless it is a

35
00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.980
small sip to take a medication. Your procedure may be canceled or rescheduled

36
00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.400
if this is not followed.

37
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.320
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying

38
00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:41.280
a petroleum-based

39
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.020
ointment or diaper rash cream can really help. That's it. You've got this.

40
00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.280
Follow the timing,

41
00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.200
finish the full dose, and stay hydrated. If you have any questions at all, don't

42
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.000
hesitate to call

43
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:59.440
our office. We're here to help.
